  "label": "a copy into a collection where its source's tombstoned delivered create holds the identity revives that create, still delivered",
  "note": "imap syncs INBOX and Archive. Archive holds basic-1@example.org as a delivered create of imap (a relocation accepted stating no handle: the provisional handle and a base naming nothing), tombstoned since by a remove held until its member is listed. A copy from INBOX takes the bare key and revives that row under the provisional handle, its base naming nothing kept: the create stays delivered, deriving nothing until the page naming its member lands it, and the held remove is withdrawn. Staged as a pending create instead, under the same provisional handle with no base, it would forget the delivery and push a second Add of a message its server already holds; given the copied body as its base, it would be no delivered create any more, as vector 221 has it for a flag change (SYNC.md sections 2, 5 and 7; STORAGE.md section 9's table, a tombstone holding a delivered create)",
